senses.gloss:
--a name of योगमाया;
1: भा. X. 2. ११.
bestows good on children when propitiated with human sacrifice; when the Goddess found the man sacrificed was a virtuous Brahmana like Bharata she became fiery and cut off the heads of the वृषल chief and his attendants who offered him to her;
2: Ib. V. 9. १२-18.
fought with निशुम्भ and शुम्भ in the देवासुर war;
3: Ib. VIII. १०. ३१.
worshipped by the गोपीस् at the end of their व्रत।
4: Ib. X. २२. 5.
Lion as her riding animal; having three eyes and a trident: praised by परशुराम;
5: Br. III. ३९. ३३, ४४ to ५३.
came out of the wrath of उमा for the destruction of the दक्ष's यज्ञ।
6: वा. ३०. १४०, १६५.

(II)--a continent of Mandara hill east of Meru; bounded on one side by गन्धमादन; traversed by the stream सीता; the capital of भद्राश्वस्, son of Dharma, engaged in the worship of हयग्रीव with due praises;
1: भा. V. १६. १०; १७. 6; १८. 1-6; M. ८३. ३१; ११३. ४४, ५२; वा. ३४. ५७; ३५. २३; Vi. III. 2. २४.
coun- try conquered by परीक्षित्;
2: भा. I. १६. १३.
people residing here are white in colour and women excell in beauty living for thousands (१०,000-वा। प्।) of years; non-injury and truth prevalent here; people here worship शङ्कर and गौरी;
3: Br. II. १५. ५०, ५७-60; वा. ४२. २४; ४३. 5-9, ११-38.
विष्णु in the form of हयशिरस्.
4: Vi. II. 2. ५०.
